NAME
    rdline - read one input line into a buffer (//#use rdline)

SYNOPSIS
    //#use stdin        (required ABOVE rdline -- provides nextc())
    //#use rdline       cc splices /lib/lib_rdline.c

DESCRIPTION
    Defines readline(), which reads up to the next LF into a caller
    buffer. (The file is named lib_rdline.c to fit P8XFS's 12-char
    filename field; the `//#use rdline` token names the FILE, not the
    function.)

    readline(buf):
      in   buf -- caller's char buffer, must hold at least 256 bytes
      out  buf gets the line's bytes (CR stripped) then a NUL
      ret  1 if a line was read, 0 if input was already at EOF

    CR (13) is dropped, so CRLF and bare-LF sources land the same. Bytes
    past 255 are discarded but still consumed, so the stream stays
    aligned to the next LF. LF (10) ends the line and is not stored. A
    partial final line with no trailing LF still returns 1.

DEPENDS ON
    lib_stdin's nextc() -- a command that uses rdline must `//#use stdin`
    ABOVE it (clib.py splices in directive order, so nextc() is defined
    before this caller). nextc()'s 65535 EOF sentinel never collides with
    a real 0..255 byte in p8cc's 16-bit int.

SEE ALSO
    stdin, sort, uniq
